@H@T0The European Forum For OS-9 (EFFO)  is    a    non-profit,    computer    andcompany independent union of idealistic OS-9/68k-users.This Help File is a quick reference to all EFFO related topics,  however,  toget full information it is recommended to participate in the EFFO forum  (seetopic "Forum").This file was last updated at December 12. 1989.  The  information  containedherein as well as the organisation of  EFFO  is  subject  to  change  withoutnotice.@D1Main_Goals : 2Forum : 3EFFO_Bierrunde : 4OS9-BBS : 5Addresses : 7Languages : 8@T2The main goals of EFFO are:   1.  Deep support for all users of OS-9/68k; advice and  problem solving       on questions about the operating system, languages, user applications       and computer specific problems.   2.  Management and taking care for all available OS-9  based  public       domain software and freeware.   3.  Promotion of contacts between OS-9 users (share experience).We turn  to  all  users  of  OS-9/68k,  professional,  amateurs  as  well  asnewcomers.@T3In an irregular rythm, EFFO produces two disks, the so  called  "forum"  withletters, programs, and other contributions from engaged OS-9 users  as   wellas  some  interesting  public domain    programs.  EFFO  also  manages  a  PDsoftware collection, which can be obtained for a small fee.Participation in the forum is free and without obligation,  but   we    shallbe pleased with anyone who will join EFFO. The member fees are used to  coverthe forum's costs. Members get rebates, for example for buying PD disks.HOW TO PARTICIPATE IN THE FORUM ?Pariticpants in the EFFO-Forum send two floppy disks  -  which  contain  yourcontribution (letter, hint, question, public domain program  etc.)  or  whichare at least formatted - together with an adhesive return  address  label  tothe EFFO editor who is responsible for your system (see topic "Addresses" forreference). If your system is capable of handling the  new  Universal  Formatfrom Microware (introduced in OS-9 2.3: 80 tracks, 16  sectors/track,  doubledensity, sector offset=1, track offset=1), then please USE  THAT  FORMAT  foryour forum disks. If you are not sure about your  disk  format,  include  allparameters you know (system type, # of tracks etc.) ON A PIECE OF  PAPER  andput some textfiles (contents don't matter, e.g. SYS/errmsgs) onto the  disks.This helps us to figure out the  disk  format;  blank  disks  are  harder  toanalyze.After we got sufficient contributions, you'll get  back  your  disks,  filledwith the forum news. Although the forum  disks  have  not  to  be  completelyfilled with data before we send  them  out,  we  don't  return  empty  disks,either. As experience shows, the  interest  in  OS-9  fades  dramatically  insummer and so does the number of contributions for the Forum.Therefore, please be patient if you have  to  wait  for  your  disks  severalmonths. We'll do our best, but we can't  do  wonders.  No  contributions,  noforum. That's the basic  rule.  It  is  clear  that  no  one  can  contributesomething every two months. But if 100 interested parties OS-9ers participatein the OS-9 forum, the probability to get enough material for an  edition  ismuch higher than if only 10 people  send  in  their  disks.  So,  aside  fromparticipating in the forum yourself, make propaganda for EFFO and  feel  freeto redistribute this help file and entire forum disks (as long as  you  don'tcharge anything, of course!!).The future of EFFO is in your hands: Send your disks now!@T4Once a month, friends of the  68000  from  Switzerland  get  together  for  ameeting which is referred to as "EFFO_Bierrunde". Despite the name, the  maintopic is OS9/68k and not beer; the name is kept mainly for historical reasons(you may drink pure H2O as well :-)Aside from OS-9, we cover hardware and computer specific themes too.   Up  tonow we have users of the following computers: Atari c't 68k,  Gepard,    GMX-Micro 20, mc 68000, VME.The "EFFO_Bierrunde" takes place every 20th of every month  except  July  andDecember. If the 20th is holiday, the meeting will be the working day closestto the 20th. Clear and simple, isn't it?For those who really indend to come: We  meet  in  the  Restaurant  Hegibach,Hegibachplatz in Zuerich. Whoever being interested in 68k and OS9 is welcome;however, be warned: The conversation is mainly swiss-german (aside  from  thetechnical terms, which are in broken english, anyway).@T5For fast information, we have the OS-9 Bulletin Board System (OS9-BBS)  whichis also a non-profit, computer independent organisation.  Although  EFFO  andthe OS9-BBS work together, the OS9-BBS is a different project of  OS9  users,supported by the Swiss Federal Institute of Technology (SFIT, ETH) of Zurich,as they put the infrastructure free of charge to our disposal.Everyone interested in OS9 can register in the OS9-BBS, and he/she  will  gethis/her own mailbox  in  order  to  communicate    with    other  users.  Forquestions, hints, etc, the OS9-BBS has an open "Conferencing  System",  whichis open to everyone as reader and as  writer.  In  (hopefully  near)  future,there will be a file system allowing  immediate  downloading  of  interestingprograms and infos.HOW TO ACCESS THE OS9-BBS:   Phone:    01/256'48'51 or 01/251'20'02     (V22, 1200bd, 8-1-N)             01/256'47'51                     (V23, 300bd, 8-1-N)             01/251'62'71                     (V22bis, 2400bd 8-1-N)             (01  is  the  area  code  of  Zurich  for  calls   from   within             Switzerland. For international access, use 00411 instead)   Telepac/Datex-P/Tymnet (X25):             (0228)479110650 or (0228)49911084101   Decnet:   xxxxxx (direct connection to host, no  "CALL  3D0"  (see  below)             required)   Login:    Wait for the #-Prompt (evtl. press RETURN)             enter CALL 3D0 <RETURN> (connection to host)             Username: OS9, Password: BULLETIN             Now the OS9-BBS-program takes over, there will be a second (BBS-             internal) User/Password request. New users may login as a  GUEST             (without password).@T7The following list contains the addresses  of  those  EFFO  editors  who  areresponsible for the different computer systems and to whom you should send  2disks for participating in the Forum (see topic "Forum").-----------------------------------------------------------------------------System    CPU       EFFO-EDITOR         Address                    Short Form-----------------------------------------------------------------------------Atari ST  68000     Philip Maechler     Grundwiesstrasse 15                PM                                        CH-8700 Kuesnacht/ZH                                        Phone: CH-1/910 41 85                                        OS9-BBS Username: MAD_USERVME/c't   680xx     Ziemowit Zglinski   Eidmattstrasse 19                  ZZ                                        CH-8049 Zuerich                                        Phone: CH-1/382 01 69                                        OS9-BBS Username: ZZZGEPARD    68010     Reto Peter          Wallisellenstrasse 483             RP                                        CH-8050 Zuerich                                        Phone W:CH-1/236 66 75,                                              P:CH-1/41 74 52                                        OS9-BBS Username: TANGRAMGimix     68020     Lukas Zeller        Hofenstrasse 12                    LZ                                        CH-8708 Maennedorf                                        Phone: CH-1/920 34 88                                        eMail: zeller@strati.ethz.ch                                        ..!mcvax!cernvax!chx400!ethz!zeller                                        DECnet: 57390::ZELLER                                        (PSI%49911084